schema: claim-evidence
object:
  title: No legitimate community will ever ask for your seed phrase
  type: claim-evidence
  claim: >-
    "No one in a real community will ever ask for your seed phrase"; a
    near-universal red flag is an unsolicited DM offering "support," a
    "giveaway," or a "verification" link.
  evidence: >-
    Article cites "security guidance from wallet makers and researchers like
    Kaspersky" and "security write-ups from Ledger and others" for both
    claims, referencing specifically Ledger Academy's "Web3 Scams Explained"
    and Kaspersky's "free seed phrase" scam writeup.
  source_lineage: >-
    src/content/docs/find-your-community.md, References: Ledger Academy
    (Web3 Scams Explained) and Kaspersky (the "free seed phrase" scam)
  interpretation: >-
    Standard, widely-corroborated web3 security guidance; low risk of being
    wrong, but presented here without direct quotation of the cited sources.
  uncertainty: >-
    The article paraphrases rather than directly quotes Ledger/Kaspersky;
    exact source wording not verified at ingestion time.
  maturity: raw
  ai_assisted: true
  provenance:
    origin: src/content/docs/find-your-community.md
    transformation: summarized
    authorship: ai-assisted
